body:
@geoand Yes, this works currently with `quarkus-resteasy` I ran into this transitioning a project over to the reactive rest easy to get kotlin coroutine support.

For anyone that runs into this issue, A work around is to make new classes with the `@Path` with the parameter on the class instead of the method.

For example, this works

```java
@Path("hello/{id}")
public class FooResource {
   @GET
   public void hello(@PathParam("id") String id) {}
}
```

This does not

```java
@Path("hello")
public class FooResource {
   @GET
   @Path("{id}")
   public void hello(@PathParam("id") String id) {}
}
```
